id: pm-edywqn
title: "The bounded legacy MCP compatibility set stops one revision short of the spec's own legacy boundary, so every current host is refused at initialize and the dual-era guarantee is unmet"
description: "Measured live on 2026-08-30 against the released stdio entrypoint plugins/pm-claude/scripts/pm-mcp-server.mjs.\n\nClaude Code 2.1.251 opens with initialize and protocolVersion 2025-11-25. The server answers JSON-RPC error -32022 'Unsupported legacy MCP protocol version' with data.supported = ['2025-06-18']. The connection never establishes. The same refusal reproduces for 2024-11-05, 2025-03-26 and, remarkably, for 2026-07-28 itself: sending the server its own canonical revision on the only entrypoint a host actually opens is answered by an unsupported-version error naming a revision two generations old.\n\nThe modern surface is healthy. A direct server/discover carrying _meta protocolVersion 2026-07-28 returns a full DiscoverResult with supportedVersions ['2026-07-28'], three negotiated extensions and instructions. So the capability exists and is unreachable through the handshake every legacy-era host uses.\n\nThe 2026-07-28 specification defines the boundary this set was supposed to track. Its Versioning and Compatibility page states the terminology directly: legacy means the versions that establish a session with an initialize handshake, namely 2025-11-25 and earlier. The compatibility matrix promises that a legacy client against a dual-era server Works, and that the server answers initialize and serves the client according to the negotiated legacy revision. pm declares itself dual-era and ships the adapter that makes that promise, but its accepted legacy set is the single literal ['2025-06-18'] and therefore omits 2025-11-25, the final and current legacy revision named by the specification pm claims conformance to.\n\nThe mechanism is a hand-maintained accept list that no gate compares against the specification's own legacy boundary. The string 2025-11-25 does not appear anywhere in src, docs, tests, plugins or packages. The legacy adapter additionally answers with PM_MCP_LEGACY_PROTOCOL_VERSIONS[0] rather than the version the client requested, so even after the set widens a client that negotiates the newer revision would be told the older one.\n\nThis is the export-map denominator family again, in the transport layer: the surface the outside world resolves is one set, and the checker consults a shorter hand list that was already stale when it was written."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:mcp",compatibility,production-defect,protocol
