author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "The accepted legacy revision set covers every initialize-era revision the referenced specification names as legacy, and 2025-11-25 is accepted; A live handshake from the released stdio entrypoint succeeds for each accepted legacy revision, proving the set is exercised end to end rather than asserted in a unit test; The initialize response echoes the revision the client negotiated rather than a fixed element of the accepted set; An unsupported request still fails and names every supported revision, so widening the set cannot be used to accept anything; A gate fails when the accepted set omits a revision the project's own conformance documentation lists as supported, so the set can never silently lag the specification again; A negative control proves the gate fails on the pre-fix accept list"
parent: pm-5k4v
risk: critical
confidence: 95
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "Every initialize-era revision the canonical specification names as legacy completes a handshake against the released stdio entrypoint, and the negotiated revision is the one the client requested."
actual_result: 2025-11-25 and 2025-06-18 both negotiate and echo the requested revision; 2024-11-05 and 2025-03-26 are refused with -32022 naming both supported revisions; Claude Code 2.1.251 reports pm-mcp Connected where it previously reported Failed to connect.
